# /handoff

Write now — end of this stage, not task start. Keep routing recommendations and their brief reason only in the short unfenced header above `PROMPT:`. Write each field as its own paragraph with exactly one blank line between fields. Keep labels plain; bold the next stage and model/effort values on RUN{{if .Both}} and eligible provider lines{{end}}.{{if .Both}} Leave below-need, insufficient-evidence and unavailable routes plain.{{end}} The fenced prompt contains only what the receiving model needs to continue: task state, constraints, exposure/shape, checks, advice, required reviews and unresolved delegation state. Do not duplicate header-only fields inside it.

## Active workflow contract

A user `/handoff` request or a received handoff activates the workflow through the stage chain. Skill loads do not carry between stages. Every receiving stage loads `delegate` before launching any advisor or worker (except a native read-only search subagent), and freshly loads `routing` together with this `handoff` skill only at END, before writing the next handoff. Mid-stage, it loads `routing` only before choosing a model (worker, advisor, discussion participant, or reroute/escalation); this handoff already routed the receiving owner. Every handoff must carry the mandatory loads in its `PROMPT:` exactly as the skeleton shows.

For a received older handoff (`RISK:`, `CONSULT *` fields, `ADVISOR ALLOWANCE HISTORY`, a counted `DELEGATION STATE`, or a mandatory load of `consult`, `dialogue` or `subagents`):
- Classify the next concrete action into `EXPOSURE:` and `SHAPE:` at stage start, without inheriting the old workflow-wide maximum.
- Load `delegate` wherever it says `consult`, `dialogue` or `subagents`.
- Carry advice conclusions into ADVICE and live children, worktrees and sessions into DELEGATION STATE.
- Preserve every condition the user stated (models{{if .Both}}, providers{{end}}, independence, coverage, timing, turn or spending limits, fallback restrictions, a declined model, "no more advice"): required reviews go in REQUIRED REVIEW, the rest in REPO CONSTRAINTS or CONTEXT. When provenance is unclear, keep the restriction until clarified.
- Drop policy-generated budget IDs, limits, counters, grants and allowance history. They create no allowance and no restriction.

For an older ranked header (`PREFERRED`, `SECONDARY`, `TERTIARY`), treat PREFERRED as the prior execution recommendation, not a permanent {{if .Both}}provider {{end}}ranking. Preserve its task, constraints and review gates; at the next handoff recompute RUN{{if .Both}} and both current provider options{{end}}. Do not reject a usable old handoff merely for its labels.

## Infer STAGE

| State | STAGE |
|---|---|
| no plan | Plan |
| unverified plan | Verify Plan |
| ready plan | Implement |
| implemented | Verify Implementation |

Without `/handoff`, work directly. Micro normally skips Plan and Verify Plan; Bounded may use an inline plan and skips separate verification unless a material decision remains. Skip a stage: same skeleton, add `SKIP TO: <stage>`, justify the skip.

## Skeleton

The header before `PROMPT:` is unfenced. Write each field as its own paragraph with exactly one blank line between fields—never combine fields on one line or in one paragraph. Keep field labels plain (e.g. write `NEXT:`, not `**NEXT:**`). Bold only the `NEXT` value and model/effort values on RUN{{if .Both}} and eligible provider lines{{end}} (`**<model>**, **<effort>**`); {{if .Both}}below-need, insufficient-evidence and unavailable routes and {{end}}`none` stay plain.{{if .Both}} Provider order is alphabetical, not a ranking. Only RUN is selected for execution; options never imply two launches.{{end}} Enclose only the content under `PROMPT:` in a ```md code fence.

REPO: <short label>

NEXT: **<next stage>**

RUN: **<model>**, **<effort>**
{{if .Both}}
CLAUDE: **<model>**, **<effort>** — <task fit; availability limit if material; unbold if ineligible>

GPT: **<model>**, **<effort>** — <task fit; availability limit if material; unbold if ineligible>
{{end}}
WHY: <{{if .Both}}best fit | comparable choices and tie-break | {{end}}declared plan allowance or observed usage limit | named choice{{if .Both}} | advisor diversity{{end}}; task-specific reason>

ESCALATE: <trigger → next suitable model and effort, or none above>

ADVISORS: <none | N question(s), complete | N question(s): <nonzero buckets only, e.g. 1 complete, 1 failed (usage limit)> | unverified (<reason>); see ADVICE>

STATE: <changed/committed/applied or blocked; one short line>

PROMPT:
```md
HANDOFF WORKFLOW: active
MANDATORY SKILLS:
- Load `delegate` before launching any advisor or worker (except a native read-only search subagent); loading it never requires a launch.
- Load `routing` mid-stage only before choosing a worker, advisor, discussion or reroute model.
- Load `routing` and `handoff` together only at END, immediately before writing the required next handoff; do not rely on a prior stage's load or summary.
REPO: <short label>
